  "findings": [
    "46 of 2612 External rows have no category: SGD 1,842.30 out and 96.40 in, 3.7 per cent of all-month spending 49,429.97.",
    "31 synthetic YouTrip rows stand in for balance jumps the export omitted; every spend and income figure excludes them.",
    "12 non-SGD row(s) sit on 1 period block(s) with no FX rate, so they are counted at face value: Y-1029384756 · JPY · 2025-03.",
    "2 month(s) have incomplete statement coverage, 2025-02 to 2025-05; every average in the other stats leaves them out.",
    "214 External rows are in a Transfer bucket, SGD 31,840.00 out. A view that filters External and forgets the bucket counts all of it as spending.",
    "The fix queue splits as 31 no rule matches, 9 no merchant text printed, 6 synthetic balance jump."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "A row with no merchant text printed can never be fixed by a rule; it needs a category typed in Notion, and the sync will not overwrite one.",
    "Synthetic rows change whenever a YouTrip month is re-exported, so their count is not stable across re-exports.",
    "Coverage is judged per account from its own first and last statement, so an account that simply had no activity looks the same as one whose statement is missing."
  ]
}
